		(property "Description" "ALINX AC7200 XC7A200T-2FBG484I Artix-7 FPGA SOM, 45x55mm, 4x 80-pin/0.5mm B2B connectors (Unit A=CON1 VCCIN/GND+BANK34+BANK13+XADC, Unit B=CON2 BANK13+BANK14, Unit C=CON3 BANK15+BANK16+JTAG (TCK/TDI/TDO/TMS on pins 77-80 -- a SEPARATE on-module 6-pin JTAG header J1 also exists, not modeled here), Unit D=CON4 BANK16+GTP transceivers). Every pin cross-checked against ALINX's own real user manual (docs/AC7200_User_Manual.pdf) -- CON2/CON3/CON4 and CON1 pins 1-72 matched an earlier web-transcription exactly; CON1 pins 73-80 (previously unverified placeholder) now filled in from the real manual. ONE correction applied: CON1 pin 27 is printed as 'B13_L7_P' in ALINX's own manual (same as pin 25) -- a real duplicate/typo in their document (different FPGA balls AB11 vs AB12, and every other one of the 320 pins alternates P/N without exception) -- corrected here to B13_L7_N. Module standalone-power (J3, 2-pin +5V/GND) and JTAG (J1, 6-pin) headers exist on the module but are not part of this symbol (carrier-board-facing CON1-4 only)."
			(at 115.57 101.6 0)
			(hide yes)
			(show_name no)
			(do_not_autoplace no)
			(effects
				(font
					(size 1.27 1.27)
				)
				(justify left)
			)
		)
